      },
      {
        "text": "Worldwide",
        "title": "Countries and Areas Deployed",
        "category": "other"
      },
      {
        "text": "Information Technology",
        "title": "Critical Infrastructure Sectors",
        "category": "other"
      },
      {
        "text": "PHP insecurely handles multiple combinations of memory allocations and error conditions. These behaviors can allow a remote attacker to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. Successful exploitation depends on a number of factors including the specific PHP application being targeted, the SAPI and web server, error handling and memory resource configuration, and platform or OS-level memory protections. Without significant analysis effort to prove otherwise, any application running on a vulnerable version of PHP should be considered vulnerable and exploitable.",
        "title": "Risk Evaluation",
        "category": "summary"
      },
      {
        "text": "These vulnerabilities are addressed in PHP versions 8.2.35, 8.3.36, 8.4.27, and 8.5.12. Additional details and mitigations can be found in this PHP advisory: [https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-21-5](https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-21-5) as well as GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w and GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp.",
        "title": "Recommended Practices",
        "category": "general"
      },
      {
        "text": "United States",
        "title": "Company Headquarters Location",
        "category": "other"
      }
    ],
